  "question": {
    "text": "Two slits are $1 \\mathrm{~mm}$ apart and the screen is located $1 \\mathrm{~m}$ away from the slits. A light of wavelength $500 \\mathrm{~nm}$ is used. The width of each slit to obtain 10 maxima of the double slit pattern within the central maximum of the single slit pattern is _____$\\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~m}$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{d}=1 \\mathrm{~mm}, \\mathrm{D}=1 \\mathrm{~m}, \\lambda=500 \\mathrm{~nm} \\\\ & 10\\left(\\frac{\\lambda \\mathrm{D}}{\\mathrm{d}}\\right)=\\frac{2 \\lambda \\mathrm{D}}{\\mathrm{a}} \\\\ & \\mathbf{a}=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{5} \\\\ &=\\frac{10 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~m}}{5} \\\\ &=2 \\times 10^{-4}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
